# Akazukin Chacha (GB, J) text table. Encoding = BG tile index of the font loaded at $9000
# (LCDC.4=0 -> codes 00-7F are tiles at $9000-$97FF; 80-EE are tiles at $8800-$8EEF, scene-dependent).
# Font: LZ-compressed at 03:$5976 (file 0xD976), 0x800 bytes -> $9000. Proven: relative search of
# on-screen dialogue (e.g. それでは = 0E 29 12 6E 19 found at 0x1A288), decode of all 1314 dialogue strings
# with zero unknown bytes, and render check (font_sheet.png / runtime VRAM dump).
# Kana order: gojuon; hiragana 00-2D (あ..ん incl. を), small ぁぃぅぇぉっゃゅょ 2E-36,
# katakana 37-64 (ア..ワヲン), small ァィゥェォッャュョ 65-6D. Dakuten 6E / handakuten 6F are SEPARATE
# characters printed in the cell AFTER the kana (が = か + ゛ = 05 6E). No digits, no Latin in the font.
# FF = blank tile (space). Codes EF-FE are control codes (dispatch table $00:3C24).
00=あ
01=い
02=う
03=え
